  "summary": "Padmasambhava, also called Guru Rinpoche, was an eighth-century Indian Buddhist master revered as the leading propagator of tantric Buddhism in Tibet. Tradition holds he went to Tibet at King Trisong Detsen's invitation and founded the Nyingma order. He is recorded as giving added help when Samye monastery was founded, around 775.",
